":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The layout is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"‘s: a perfect binary tree over the values padded to a power of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two, in one flat array of cells. Beside each internal cell sits a pending update, applied to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that cell’s value but not yet to the cells below it. A range update applies itself to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") cells that cover the range and leaves it pending there, pushing older pending","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"updates down one level on the way so that updates reach each cell in the order they were made.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A query reads without changing the tree, composing the pending updates of the cells it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"passes through.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names the monoid and the updates:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["enum AddToSum: MonoidAction {","    typealias Values = Sum<Int>","    static var identity: Int { 0 }","    static func compose(_ outer: Int, _ inner: Int) -> Int { outer + inner }","    static func apply(_ update: Int, to sum: Int, count: Int) -> Int { sum + update * count }","}","","var tree = LazySegmentTree<AddToSum>([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])","tree.apply(10, in: 1 ..< 4)","tree.combined(in: 0 ..< 5)   \/\/ 45","tree[2]                      \/\/ 13"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","in